6: attacks e4, g4, h5, h7, d5, d7 — not g1.\n\nSo neither f1 nor g1 is under attack. Therefore, **castling kingside is safe**.\n\nReason: Castling is one of the highest-priority moves in the opening/middlegame: it secures the king, activates the rook, and is often the most efficient way to improve position. With all conditions met and no risk, it is superior to slow development or pawn pushes.\n\nAnswer: K: e1-g1'}
