o support an attack or reposition toward f5 or g6.\n- B: f6-g7 puts immediate pressure on the black king at f7, potentially threatening discovered attacks or pinning if supported.\n- However, N: c6-e7 stands out—it develops the knight to a strong square, eyes f5 and d5, supports potential central control, and avoids blocking the c-pawn.\n\nBut most promising is **B: f6-g7** — this move places the bishop on a strong diagonal directly targeting the black king on f7. It creates immediate pressure and threatens discovered checks if combined with rook lifts or knight maneuvers. Additionally, it may force Black to respond defensively, giving me initiative.\n\nReason: B: f6-g7 increases activity, targets the exposed black king, and contributes to a quick attacking plan. It’s one of the few moves that create immediate threats, maximizing winning chances.\n\nAnswer: B: f6-g7'}
